Z||000009||Monkeyman||12-14-1999||09:54 PM||||superX--there's a thread about them. Try "Search".  Basically, just click on the "Pennocks Image Poster" icon on the bottom of your screen.  Download that and follow the instructions.  The white looks cool.  I'd like to see the other colors, too.  And what's the difference between the backlit and reflector type gauges?  I thought all of them were the same.||||reg||1
Z||000010||superXmotorsports||12-14-1999||10:25 PM||||Thanks for posting the pic GREENDANO.  They are backlit and in red.  Slightly deeper red than stock, very close to the illumination in new Pontiac Firebirds.  I have (1) yellow set in stock (that I posted in MALL section) the orange and red would be special order.<BR>Thanks. SXM.||||reg||14
Z||000011||Scott2M4||12-15-1999||07:00 AM||||<B>OH YA!!!!!</B>  I want those <B>BAD!!!!!</B><P>Reflector vs backlit?  Others will do better at explaining this but I'll try.  Reflector style are solid faces with number and symbol decals attached.  The light is generated behind the gauge but reflected around the edges of the dial and projected onto the face.  Backlit style are faces with transparent numbers and symbols.  The light is generated behind the gauge but seen through the transparent images.  Backlit gauges are more dramatic and easier to read.<P>As far as which cars have which gauge, I believe all V6 cars got the backlit style and all 4 cylinder cars got the reflector style.||||reg||4
Z||000012||Wolfhound||12-15-1999||07:34 AM||||When you remove the needles to apply these faces, how do you reposition them correctly?<BR>I have a 86, 120mph, set that the needle has fallen off the Tach. I know they don't return to zero stop. there doesn't appear to be a register on the shaft.<BR>Coy||||reg||5
Z||000013||superXmotorsports||12-15-1999||08:17 AM||||When you remove the needle to remove the current black face you replace the needle in the same location as you removed the old one (it's best to do one at a time).  With the tach you remove the peg first and the needle will sweep to about the 3 O'clock position.  Try positioning your needle there and then install and check your idle RPM for accuracy.<P>These gauges are only designed for the V6 and the speedo is 120MPH.  Thanks.  SXM.||||reg||1
Z||000014||Wolfhound||12-15-1999||08:27 AM||||Thanks, I have an 85 GT V6 that has the 80 MPH speedo I want to put the whole cluster in from an 86 GT parts car.<BR>I,ll give that a try. The white gages look great.<BR>Coy||||reg||1
Z||000015||BOILERMAKER||12-15-1999||10:55 AM||||OK, looks good -- lasts a long time.<P>I want them (well, after my list is widdled down a little bit) but where would I get them?||||reg||1
Z||000016||william_thorniii||12-15-1999||01:24 PM||||Hey Super,<P>Are you going to be producing them with different color light?  I want white face guages but intend on changing the color that is transmitted by the bulb.  I realize that doing this is as easy as painting the bulbs, but wasn't sure if it would be a purchase option or not.<P>Many Thanks,<P>William T. Thorn, III||||reg||5
Z||000017||superXmotorsports||12-15-1999||01:30 PM||||I carry those.  I normally have the white.  I have (1) set of yellow in stock.  I can also get orange or red for those interested.  Retail is $125 includes all 6 gauge faces for V6 cars / 120MPH speedo.  I will install for $30 additional is you send in your cluster.  I may have a special price for Forum members - I'm working on it (I didn't know that many people were interested).  If you have further questions you can email me directly.  Thanks.  SXM.||||reg||3
Z||000018||superXmotorsports||12-15-1999||01:33 PM||||To answer William - all the gauges glow deep red at night, that is the color of the material they are constructed from.  All the gauges they produce for other cars are made from the same material.  SXM.||||reg||1
Z||000019||Wolfhound||12-15-1999||01:47 PM||||The reasoning behind red as a night guage color is that it causes very little retnia fatique, My cabinlights in my sailboat are red for this reason. I can sail at night with them on without it effecting my night vision.  I,ve thought of backing the overheads in my Fiero with the emergency taillight tape for the same reason. It would allow your passenger to look at a map or whatever while driving at night safely. ||||reg||1
Z||000020||Eric||12-15-1999||02:58 PM||||They look pretty good.  I might be interested.  How do the needles contrast against the white background?  And does the entire background turn red with black lettering?  I think that may look a little weird.  Maybe we should see a picture at night with the lights turned on.||||reg||1
Z||000021||william_thorniii||12-15-1999||05:59 PM||||I fully understand the advantages of red hues on instrumentation.  Beyond the fatigue, they also are almost exclusively used in jets because they appear sharper.  I however am concerned neither with fatigue nor sharpness.  I am concerned about asthetics.  I will simply proceed with home customization.  I find it funny that although red gages are superior scientifically so few vehicles are equipt with red gages.  <P>William T. Thorn, III||||reg||1
Z||000022||superXmotorsports||12-15-1999||08:38 PM||||Eric - the NUMBERS glow red the gauge appears black.  I had installed these in my 99 Spyder last year and loved them - so I shopped for someone to make them for the Fiero.  The needle looks at home during the day on the white background (you can see it a little in the pic).  I hadn't intended on putting them out for the masses until after the 1st of the year.  I will have a special Forum price to post by tomorrow evening.  SXM.<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000023||superXmotorsports||12-15-1999||08:42 PM||||Wolfhound - you can now buy red wedge bulbs to replace your overhead light bulbs.  I replace 1 set with red and the other with stock bulbs that way you have a choice. SXM.||||reg||14
Z||000024||Wolfhound||12-15-1999||08:46 PM||||Red gauges aren't critical in cars where you are meeting white light head on most of the time. I find them easy to read and less disruptive than say blue or green. Asthetics are important also. At 53 I,m concerned with retnia fatique :-) <BR> It may be possible to repaint the back side of the guage housing a different color to change the reflective color. I,ve never tried it but maybe someone here has. It,s a thought anyway! I think the backlit guages are printed on a translucent red plastic.<p>[This message has been edited by Wolfhound (edited 12-15-1999).]||||reg||7
Z||000025||Wolfhound||12-15-1999||09:03 PM||||Good shot on the choice of red or white light. My boat is set up with both.<BR>Thanks<BR>Coy||||reg||14
